###  http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Phoret
:physioChemicalPropertyCode-Phoret rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                            <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalCompound> ,
                                            <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalSubstance> ,
                                            :PhysioChemicalPropertyCode ,
                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                                   <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/inchi> "1S/P" ;
                                   <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/pubchem> "5462309.0" ;
                                   <http://dbpedia.org/property/inchikey> "OAICVXFJPJFONN-UHFFFAOYSA-N" ;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> :PhysioChemicalPropertyCollection ;
                                   rdfs:seeAlso <https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5462309.0> ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Phosphorus retention measures a soil's capacity to adsorb and hold phosphorus, influenced by soil texture, pH, and mineralogy. While high retention reduces leaching, it may also limit phosphorus availability to plants. Understanding phosphorus retention helps optimize fertilization and minimize environmental impacts. Source: Brady & Weil (2017). ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/> ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "Phoret" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Phosphorus (P) - retention"@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/isPropertyOf> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Horizon> ,
                                                                           <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Layer> .


###  http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Photot
:physioChemicalPropertyCode-Photot rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                            <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalCompound> ,
                                            <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/ChemicalSubstance> ,
                                            :PhysioChemicalPropertyCode ,
                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                                   <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/inchi> "1S/P" ;
                                   <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/pubchem> "5462309.0" ;
                                   <http://dbpedia.org/property/inchikey> "OAICVXFJPJFONN-UHFFFAOYSA-N" ;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> :PhysioChemicalPropertyCollection ;
                                   rdfs:seeAlso <https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5462309.0> ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Total phosphorus includes all forms of phosphorus in the soil, both organic and inorganic. While only a fraction is plant-available, total phosphorus serves as a long-term reserve for crop nutrition. Adequate phosphorus levels are crucial for energy transfer, photosynthesis, and root development in plants. Source: Soil Chemistry by Bohn et al. ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/> ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "Photot" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Phosphorus (P) - total"@en ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/isPropertyOf> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Horizon> ,
                                                                           <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Layer> .


###  http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/physioChemicalPropertyCode-Por
:physioChemicalPropertyCode-Por rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                         :PhysioChemicalPropertyCode ,
                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> :PhysioChemicalPropertyCollection ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Porosity refers to the percentage of soil volume occupied by pores or voids, which hold air and water. It directly impacts water infiltration, drainage, and root growth. Soils with high porosity are better suited for crop cultivation, as they provide good aeration and water availability. Source: Brady & Weil (2017). ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 3,ISRIC Report 2014/01: Africa Soil Profiles Database Version 1.2. Annex 3a" ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/properties/> ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "Por" ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Porosity"@en ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/isPropertyOf> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Horizon> ,
                                                                        <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/layerhorizon/GL_Layer> .


